    "body": "Nuclear power group AMPERA and Berto Acquisition Corp. jointly announced that the companies have entered into a definitive agreement for a business combination. The transaction implies an equity value for AMPERA of about $900 million on a pre-money equity.\nAMPERA develops scalable power solutions for data center, defense, industrial, and maritime applications. As part of its business strategy, AMPERA is pursuing near-term commercial power generation using heat recovery and conventional fuels through its PowerNOW program, while simultaneously conducting longer-term development of advanced nuclear technology through its NuclearNEXT approach. AMPERA is combining advanced manufacturing, artificial intelligence (AI), emerging quantum computing capabilities and next-generation energy technologies to develop reliable, highly efficient, factory-built power systems.\nBerto is a publicly traded special purpose acquisition company. The group said that in connection with the business combination with AMPERA, it has entered into subscription agreements with certain institutional and accredited investors and strategic investors. Pursuant to the PIPE Subscription Agreements, Berto has agreed to issue and sell, and the subscribers agreed to subscribe for and purchase at closing, in a private placement, an aggregate of about $30 million of shares of Class A common stock of the post-merger combined company. The stock would be at a per share price equal to the price at which Berto’s public shares may be redeemed in connection with the business combination.\nIn addition to the PIPE financing, AMPERA has closed or received commitments for an additional $10 million in pre-transaction close equity and debt financing, bringing total capital commitments in excess of $40 million to date. The PIPE and the company’s existing investors include a leading AI data center equipment provider, one of the world’s largest quantum computing companies, a global maritime company, a U.S. defense contractor, and a Middle East industrial investor.\nBerto and AMPERA are in discussions with a number of strategic and institutional investors regarding an additional $50 million to $100 million of PIPE capital. No definitive agreements have been signed for this additional capital, there is no assurance it will be raised, and the final amount may be higher or lower. Any additional capital would be incremental to the PIPE described above, and the transaction is not conditioned on its being raised.\nThe minimum cash condition in the transaction is set at the final PIPE raise amount. Accordingly, the transaction has no minimum cash condition above the amount of PIPE capital raised. For illustrative purposes, assuming $100 million of additional PIPE capital and no redemptions, gross capital available to AMPERA could exceed $450 million.\nUpon closing, which is subject to approval by the stockholders of both AMPERA and Berto, receipt of required regulatory approvals and satisfaction or waiver of customary closing conditions, including the minimum cash condition described above, the combined company is expected to be named “AMPERA, Inc.” and is anticipated to list on the Nasdaq Stock Market under the ticker symbol “AMPR,” subject to Nasdaq approval. The transaction is currently expected to close in the first quarter of 2027, although there can be no assurance regarding the timing or completion of the transaction. AMPERA intends to use expected proceeds from the transaction to fund its platform development and initial commercial scale-up, although the amount of proceeds available to the combined company will depend on, among other things, the level of redemptions by Berto’s shareholders and the total amount of financing raised.\n“This transaction represents a defining milestone for AMPERA as we work to bring our advanced energy technologies to market,” said Brian Matthews, founder and CEO of AMPERA. “The rapid growth of AI infrastructure, data centers and industrial electrification is creating unprecedented demand for reliable, scalable power. Our PowerNOW platform is designed to address that demand through modular, high-efficiency power generation systems, with initial commercial deliveries targeted for 2027. In parallel, our NuclearNEXT program is advancing a fundamentally different approach to nuclear energy through a source-assisted, subcritical thorium architecture. We believe the combination of near-term commercial opportunities and longer-term nuclear innovation creates a compelling foundation for significant growth.”\nAMPERA is developing a proprietary supercritical carbon dioxide (sCO 2 ) platform, the sPower power conversion cycle. The sPower technology is applicable across PowerNOW solutions, gas turbine bottoming cycles, industrial heat recovery and eventually NuclearNEXT.\nAMPERA’s PowerNOW strategy provides fuel flexibility, efficiency and deployability advantages. The company currently plans to offer four configurations:\nAMP-G7.5: AMPERA’s initial natural-gas-fired system utilizing sPower, targeting 7.5MW net electrical output and commercial production in Q4 2027.\nAMP-G15: The next-generation evolution of AMP-G7.5, utilizing an enhanced sPower conversion system, targeting 15MW net electrical output.\nsPower Heat Recovery: For use in industrial waste heat recovery, efficient bottoming cycle on gas turbines and other third-party heat sources.\nPowerNOW Gas Turbine Variant: A higher-capacity configuration under development that integrates a conventional gas turbine with AMPERA’s proprietary sPower bottoming cycle, targeting up to 45MW total electrical output.\nUnder its NuclearNEXT strategy, AMPERA is developing the AMP-N15 to include a proprietary thorium-fueled, factory-sealed reactor based on a source-assisted subcritical architecture that targets 15MW net electrical output and an up-to 30-year core life with no routine refueling.\n“We believe the combined entity will create significant value for shareholders by capturing what we see as a transformational market opportunity,” said Harry L. You, executive chairman of Berto Acquisition Corp. “AMPERA is uniquely positioned to lead the commercialization of near-term power production and the industrialization of nuclear energy at scale, serving the power demand from AI data centers, defense applications, maritime and industrial users. The AMPERA nuclear platform distinctively combines subcritical architecture, thorium fuel, no refueling, environmentally friendly non-water based cooling, and factory manufacturing in a single system. We have great confidence in the leadership of Brian Matthews and his team.”\nNeedham & Company, LLC is serving as financial advisor to AMPERA and as placement agent for the PIPE transaction. Sichenzia Ross Ference Carmel LLP is serving as legal advisor to AMPERA. White & Case LLP is serving as legal advisor to Berto.\n—This content was contributed by the communications team for AMPERA .\nTagged in:\nAMPERA\nBerto\nbusiness combination\nfinance\nnuclear\ntransaction",
